{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function toHttpStream(\n   stream, \n   abortController?, \ngetId?): ReadableStream<Uint8Array<ArrayBufferLike>>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts#L1227","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts:1227"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convert a StreamChunk async iterable to a ReadableStream in HTTP stream format (newline-delimited JSON)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This creates a ReadableStream that emits chunks as newline-delimited JSON:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each chunk is JSON.stringify'd and followed by \"\\n\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No SSE formatting (no \"data: \" prefix)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This format is compatible with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchHttpStream"},{"type":"text","value":" connection adapter."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getId"},{"type":"text","value":" is supplied (delivery durability), each chunk is emitted as an\nenvelope "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{\"id\":\"<offset>\",\"chunk\":{…}}"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of a bare chunk. NDJSON has\nno native event-id field like SSE's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id:"},{"type":"text","value":" line, so the resumable offset rides\ninside the payload. Untagged chunks (no id) stay bare, so a non-durable\nstream is byte-identical to before and the client auto-detects either form."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"stream","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stream"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AsyncIterable"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AGUIEvent.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGUIEvent"}]},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AsyncIterable of StreamChunks from chat()"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"abortcontroller","children":[{"type":"text","value":"abortController?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortController"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional AbortController to abort when stream is cancelled"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"getId?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"index"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional per-chunk durability offset; when present, chunks are envelope-encoded"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReadableStream"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Uint8Array"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ArrayBufferLike"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ReadableStream in HTTP stream format (newline-delimited JSON)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const stream = chat({ adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'), messages: [...] });\nconst readableStream = toHttpStream(stream);\n// Use with Response for HTTP streaming (not SSE)\nreturn new Response(readableStream, {\n  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-ndjson' }\n});","lang":"typescript"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"stream","text":"stream","level":3},{"id":"abortcontroller","text":"abortController?","level":3},{"id":"getid","text":"getId?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction toHttpStream(\n   stream, \n   abortController?, \ngetId?): ReadableStream<Uint8Array<ArrayBufferLike>>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts:1227](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts#L1227)\n\nConvert a StreamChunk async iterable to a ReadableStream in HTTP stream format (newline-delimited JSON)\n\nThis creates a ReadableStream that emits chunks as newline-delimited JSON:\n- Each chunk is JSON.stringify'd and followed by \"\\n\"\n- No SSE formatting (no \"data: \" prefix)\n\nThis format is compatible with `fetchHttpStream` connection adapter.\n\nWhen `getId` is supplied (delivery durability), each chunk is emitted as an\nenvelope `{\"id\":\"<offset>\",\"chunk\":{…}}` instead of a bare chunk. NDJSON has\nno native event-id field like SSE's `id:` line, so the resumable offset rides\ninside the payload. Untagged chunks (no id) stay bare, so a non-durable\nstream is byte-identical to before and the client auto-detects either form.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### stream\n\n`AsyncIterable`\\<[`AGUIEvent`](../type-aliases/AGUIEvent.md)\\>\n\nAsyncIterable of StreamChunks from chat()\n\n### abortController?\n\n`AbortController`\n\nOptional AbortController to abort when stream is cancelled\n\n### getId?\n\n(`chunk`, `index`) => `string` \\| `undefined`\n\nOptional per-chunk durability offset; when present, chunks are envelope-encoded\n\n## Returns\n\n`ReadableStream`\\<`Uint8Array`\\<`ArrayBufferLike`\\>\\>\n\nReadableStream in HTTP stream format (newline-delimited JSON)\n\n## Example\n\n```typescript\nconst stream = chat({ adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'), messages: [...] });\nconst readableStream = toHttpStream(stream);\n// Use with Response for HTTP streaming (not SSE)\nreturn new Response(readableStream, {\n  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-ndjson' }\n});\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: toHttpStream\ntitle: toHttpStream\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction toHttpStream(\n   stream, \n   abortController?, \ngetId?): ReadableStream<Uint8Array<ArrayBufferLike>>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts:1227](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts#L1227)\n\nConvert a StreamChunk async iterable to a ReadableStream in HTTP stream format (newline-delimited JSON)\n\nThis creates a ReadableStream that emits chunks as newline-delimited JSON:\n- Each chunk is JSON.stringify'd and followed by \"\\n\"\n- No SSE formatting (no \"data: \" prefix)\n\nThis format is compatible with `fetchHttpStream` connection adapter.\n\nWhen `getId` is supplied (delivery durability), each chunk is emitted as an\nenvelope `{\"id\":\"<offset>\",\"chunk\":{…}}` instead of a bare chunk. NDJSON has\nno native event-id field like SSE's `id:` line, so the resumable offset rides\ninside the payload. Untagged chunks (no id) stay bare, so a non-durable\nstream is byte-identical to before and the client auto-detects either form.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### stream\n\n`AsyncIterable`\\<[`AGUIEvent`](../type-aliases/AGUIEvent.md)\\>\n\nAsyncIterable of StreamChunks from chat()\n\n### abortController?\n\n`AbortController`\n\nOptional AbortController to abort when stream is cancelled\n\n### getId?\n\n(`chunk`, `index`) => `string` \\| `undefined`\n\nOptional per-chunk durability offset; when present, chunks are envelope-encoded\n\n## Returns\n\n`ReadableStream`\\<`Uint8Array`\\<`ArrayBufferLike`\\>\\>\n\nReadableStream in HTTP stream format (newline-delimited JSON)\n\n## Example\n\n```typescript\nconst stream = chat({ adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'), messages: [...] });\nconst readableStream = toHttpStream(stream);\n// Use with Response for HTTP streaming (not SSE)\nreturn new Response(readableStream, {\n  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-ndjson' }\n});\n```\n"}
